  "event:evt.gen_28.esau_marries_mahalath": {
   "status": "approved",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "skill": "urim-chronologist@5",
    "run": "main"
   },
   "produced_at": "2026-11-02T13:48:23+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [
    "The text gives no time. 28:6–9 are in pluperfect/flashback form ('Esau saw that Isaac had blessed Jacob and sent him'), so I place the marriage after the departure ends, offset 20 days with margin 20 days so the window lies wholly after Jacob has left, as a sequence estimate. Ishmael is already dead per evt.gen_25.ishmael_death (c. 1944 BCE); 'went to Ishmael' is read as to Ishmael's house/family, and Mahalath was given by her family. Chronology of Ishmael's death against Esau's marriage is a tension for the reviewer."
   ],
   "history": [
    {
     "status": "changes_requested",
     "at": "2026-11-02T13:47:33+00:00",
     "note": "[should_fix] In narrative_summary write 'He goes to Ishmael and takes Mahalath…' as the verse says, and keep the question of Ishmael's death (25:17) in temporal_reasoning_note. (GEN.28.9: \"וַיֵּלֶךְ עֵשָׂו אֶל־יִשְׁמָעֵאל\" (\"Then went Esau unto Ishmael\")) [should_fix] Make the offset at least as large as the margin (for example offset 20 days, margin 20 days), or anchor on the departure END, so that the whole window falls after Jacob has left. (GEN.28.6–7: \"Esau saw that Isaac had blessed Jacob, and sent him away… and that Jacob… was gone to Padan-aram\")",
     "by": "urim-critic@3 · claude-opus-5-5"
    },
    {
     "status": "approved",
     "at": "2026-11-02T13:49:14+00:00",
     "note": null,
     "by": "urim-critic@3 · claude-opus-5-5"
    }
   ],
   "source": null
  },
