    "Journey Beersheba–Bethel is 84 km straight, ~106 km by road; `urim travel` on foot gives ~3 days. The text has Jacob reach the place at sunset ('the sun had set'). Targum Pseudo-Jonathan 28:10 says the day was shortened and he arrived the very day he left (a miracle); I follow the ordinary walking count and keep the Targum as a variant. Isaac's home is taken as Beersheba (26:23, 26:33). The departure day is not stated: I put it one day after the charge, margin two days."
   ],
